  "text": "term Ratio Scale One of the four basic levels of measurement , a ratio scale is a numerical scale with a true zero point and in which a given size interval has the same interpretation for the entire scale. Weight is a ratio scale, Therefore, it is meaningful to say that a 200 pound person weighs twice as much as a 100 pound person.",
